0187: blueline speaker stage 3: GLINK to the ADSP, APR, a test tone (bluesnd=3)

bluesnd=3 boots the ADSP (0186), opens GLINK on the lpass edge and the
apr_audio_svc channel, then: AVCS ready, the amps booted and configured
(0x40 TDM slot 1, 0x41 slot 0), QUAT TDM pins and port started, amps
powered, an ASM stream through an ADM COPP to QUAT_TDM_RX_0, and 1 kHz for
bluesnd_secs (3) at bluesnd_amp (1000/32767). The PCM buffer is 64 KiB at
0xe1000000 behind an identity SMMU bank for stream 0x1821.

Also: blueline_bbi2c buses are shared by pins and serialized (the gauge and
the amps use GPIO 49/50); blueline_wifi.c exports its SMMU identity-bank
setup as blueline_smmu_identity().

